    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6a01e109-c749-54f1-9e26-a2c77a324840",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $3?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $A$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $B$ since it has only $2$ rows (and only $2$ columns).\n\n- $E$ since it has only $2$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns, while the matrix $D$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=3$ and $\\text{rank}(D)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $C.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e025e7c0-3d62-56e5-8b28-ac8cbc92bd85",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "c819cc3a-ae47-54d5-984a-6ce80f0cdaa6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b6381438-5910-5498-99cb-545adb8cc4e1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "fa6d72d0-dac7-5e2c-8c91-534dd1249d4e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "4c90aa49-6bd9-5112-9a6c-e6c90e61712f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "0c63789d-0203-5ed5-ae79-4a178ca3de48",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "fa6d72d0-dac7-5e2c-8c91-534dd1249d4e"
          ]
        }
      ]
